      "description": "Kolte-Patil Developers Ltd on Tuesday reported a 52 per cent growth in sales bookings to Rs 1,019 crore in the July-September quarter on better demand for its housing projects.\nIts sales bookings stood at Rs 670 crore in the year-ago period.\nIn a regulatory filing, the company reported its highest-ever quarterly sales of Rs 1,019 crore in the July-September period of  2026-27 fiscal, up 52 per cent year-on-year.\nFor the first half of this fiscal, sales bookings reached a record Rs 1,636 crore, up 27 per cent from Rs 1,286 crore in the year-ago period.\nHrishikesh Parandekar, Chief Executive Officer, Kolte-Patil Developers, said, \"Our robust performance in Q2 and H1 FY27, with record quarterly and half-yearly sales and strong collections, reflects the resilience of our business.\"\nThe company saw strong sales in new projects and also sustained sales across its ongoing projects, he added.  \"While demand has softened in the near term across the broader market, particularly in Pune, we",
